# Frontend Core Standards

- Prioritize maintainability, readability, scalability, accessibility, and responsive behavior.
- Avoid hacks and temporary solutions unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly changes it.
- Prefer small focused modifications over large rewrites.
- Inspect surrounding architecture before implementing changes.
- Separate UI, business logic, API logic, hooks, and utilities.
- Avoid duplicated logic.
- Avoid business logic directly inside JSX.

## Project organization

Prefer this structure:

```text
src/
  api/
  assets/
  components/
  features/
  hooks/
  layouts/
  pages/
  routes/
  styles/
  utils/

## Naming
- Use descriptive and intention-revealing names.
- Avoid abbreviations unless universally understood.
- Use kebab-case for IDs.
- Use PascalCase for React components.
- Use camelCase for variables and functions.

## Code quality
- Remove dead code and unused imports.
- Avoid magic strings and magic numbers.
- Keep files reasonably small and cohesive.
- Do not mix unrelated refactors with feature work.

